// m2r_row (row.id) pushes one blank row onto phiof and one onto outv, and
// that is its whole effect, so a case can only see it through a reader of
// one of those tables -- and a reader can only tell the push apart from the
// reset that precedes it from a state where the tables are not empty.
// optfx_setup (../../../run/pipe/cases/optfx.id) leaves both at zero.

m2r_row_fixture() {
  optfx_setup();
  m2r_row();
} return void;
():() then calls optfx_setup:[1]
():() then len((import phiof)):(1)

// outv is written in place: m2r_kept (../../walk/body/scan/ldst.id),
// m2r_seed1 and m2r_phi_make each lset a cell of a row m2r_row already
// pushed, so neither the table's length nor any row's changes, and outv_len
// witnesses none of them. One sum over every cell witnesses all three. It
// says a cell changed, not which, and because the values written here are
// instruction ids rather than counts, two writes that cancelled would leave
// the total where it was.
outv_sum() {
  int n = 0;
  int i = 0;
  while(i < len((import outv))) {
    n = n + list_sum((import outv)[i]);
    i = i + 1;
  }
} chain () {
  string outv_t = "outv " + n;
} return string outv_t;
given m2r_row_fixture ():("outv 0")
given m2r_outv_fixture ():("outv -1")

